%% BL-891 added a master-main-reconcile sweep to the same handoffd.bb
%% cadence, mirroring BL-356's push-sweep! in the opposite direction:
%% origin/main's landed commits never reached the master checkout's own
%% local main ref (QA can only `git push origin HEAD:main`; git refuses to
%% update a branch checked out in another worktree, and the coordinator is
%% constitutionally forbidden any git merge/push), so every landing left
%% the master checkout further behind and, once it also carried local
%% bookkeeping commits, genuinely diverged. The sweep merges origin/main
%% forward into local main whenever no dirty (or untracked) path overlaps a
%% path the merge would itself change (BL-919 narrowed this from a blanket
%% any-dirt gate); an actual overlap or a merge conflict blocks it and
%% surfaces a note to the coordinator instead
%% of touching the checkout.
%% BL-897 added a lifecycle-snapshot sweep to the same handoffd.bb cadence,
%% immediately ahead of the briefing sections it feeds: ensure-lifecycle-
%% snapshot! runs emit-lifecycle-snapshot.js at most once per UTC day and
%% writes a machine-local .swarmforge/briefing/lifecycle-snapshot.json
%% (gitignored, never committed), which the cost-health sidecar, digest-line
%% and open-ticket-chart briefing CLIs are then all handed via a --snapshot
%% flag so one send's sections read the identical ticket-lifecycle records
%% instead of each re-walking the backlog's full git history. A missing,
%% unreadable or stale snapshot degrades a consumer straight back to its own
%% walk, exactly as it worked before this sweep existed.
%% BL-678 added a batch-claim-progress suspect sweep to the same handoffd.bb
%% cadence: batch-mode claims (cleaner, hardener) now write a
%% .batch-claim-progress.json sidecar the instant ready_for_next_batch.bb
%% claims a parcel (owner role, claim/last-progress instants, last-seen
%% commit) - closing the live-owner half of BL-648's source near-miss (a
%% batch claim with no progress record nearly caused a duplicate
%% re-forward). The sweep refreshes the sidecar from the owning worktree's
%% HEAD and, past a staleness threshold with no advance, surfaces a named
%% suspect note to the coordinator - report-only, same posture as the
%% dropped-parcel sweep; it never re-forwards or re-delivers the parcel
%% itself, and never becomes a liveness oracle for a dead owner (BL-648's
%% job) or touches BL-528's task-mode claim-idle ladder.
